    "updated_at": "2024-03-05T01:06:16Z",
    "body": "I think registration is correct.  Arguably the current use of registration allows the spec to hand-wave the lack of steps like the [push API's deactivation text](https://w3c.github.io/push-api/#subscription-deactivation).\r\n\r\nGiven the [removal of registration resurrection from the SW spec](https://github.com/w3c/ServiceWorker/pull/1415), and because the [SW job queue mechanism does operate in terms of scopes](https://w3c.github.io/ServiceWorker/#dfn-scope-to-job-queue-map), specifying persistent notification in terms of scope I think ends up much more constraining for implementations because notifications would inherently need to run a set of steps as part of the ServiceWorker unregister job.   (Although I suppose this is already the case for push citing [registration clearing](https://w3c.github.io/ServiceWorker/#clear-registration-algorithm).)\r\n\r\nThat said, I think the notifications spec could benefit from additional clarity like the push deactivation text.",
